  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING: Status and Problem are now [JsonIgnore] on Result/Result<T> — they no longer appear in the serialized response body. Consumers reading these fields from the JSON must use the HTTP status code (Status) and ProblemDetails body (Problem) instead.\n\t\t\tBREAKING: ListResult<T> is now unwrappable — its response body is the inner array, not the wrapper object. PagedResult<T> stays wrapped (keeps PageNumber/TotalPages metadata).\n\t\t\tFixed a latent bug where IResultData.Data returned null for ListResult<T> (data was never forwarded to the base Result).\n\t\t\tAdded ProblemBuilder: a fluent builder for ProblemResult with WithTitle/WithType/WithDescription/WithDetail/WithInstance and AddExtension(s).\n\t\t\tWithDetail and WithInstance map to the RFC 9457 \"detail\" and \"instance\" members (stored as extensions until promoted to top-level properties).",
